d Services. The rates of monthly basic pay (37 U.S.C. \n203(a)) for members of the uniformed services, as adjusted under 37 U.S.C. \n1009, and the rate of monthly cadet or midshipman pay (37 U.S.C. 203(c)) \nare set forth on Schedule 8 attached hereto and made a part hereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"88 FR 89259, PDF pages 1-12; Sec. 4","sha256":"77faa72db116c1cfbc27d8a11a7bdd8886ebd892522695943bed1d5398a0d635","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2023-12-26/pdf/2023-28661.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14113#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Pursuant to section 5304 of title 5, United States Code, and my authority \nto implement an alternative level of comparability payments under section \n5304a of title 5, United States Code, locality-based comparability payments \nshall be paid in accordance with Schedule 9 attached hereto and made \na part hereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"88 FR 89259, PDF pages 1-12; Sec. 5(a)","sha256":"77faa72db116c1cfbc27d8a11a7bdd8886ebd892522695943bed1d5398a0d635","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2023-12-26/pdf/2023-28661.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14113#sec5(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Director of the Office of Personnel Management shall take such \nactions as may be necessary to implement these payments and to publish \nappropriate notice of such payments in the Federal Register.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"88 FR 89259, PDF pages 1-12; Sec. 5(b)","sha256":"77faa72db116c1cfbc27d8a11a7bdd8886ebd892522695943bed1d5398a0d635","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2023-12-26/pdf/2023-28661.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14113#sec5(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 6. Administrative Law Judges. Pursuant to section 5372 of title 5, \nUnited States